<title>EGYPT: Milling firm paying out 3.03 pounds.</title>
<headline>Milling firm paying out 3.03 pounds.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-01-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Central Egypt Flour Mills said on Sunday it was paying an annual dividend of 3.03 pounds a share for the financial year 1995/6, which ended June 30.</p>
<p>The company said results in the first half of 1996/7 were excellent and it expected the 1996/7 dividend to be higher. It will announce those results later this month.</p>
<p>The company said in November it made net after-tax profits of 41.842 million pounds ($12.3 million) in 1995/6, up on 24.887 million in the previous year.</p>
<p>$1=3.40 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
